fraction\": 1.0,\n    \"layout_rationale\": \"The inspected ICLR style has one 5.5-inch text column. A shallow 5.5 by about 1.55-inch overview on page 1 or 2 gives three stages enough room for 9-point labels without turning the figure into a dense algorithm listing.\",\n    \"allow_progression\": false,\n    \"max_panels\": 1,\n    \"max_panels_per_row\": 1,\n    \"max_categories_per_panel\": 6,\n    \"max_series_per_panel\": 3,\n    \"intended_footprint\": \"Approximately 0.22 body page including caption; three stages within one cohesive panel, not three separate subfigures.\",\n    \"content_budget\": \"At most six labeled nodes, three method-color keys, short stage titles, and no measured-looking toy scatter or invented region sizes. A simplex icon is conceptual, explicitly not experimental data.\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n    ],\n    \"export_requirements\": \"Editable draw.io source and deterministic export; use a PDF if produced from source. The designated workflow may be raster-only, in which case regenerate at at least 2400 px wide, never upscale.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"figure_id\": \"coverage_volume_by_regime\",\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"purpose\": \"Expose regime-specific benefits and failures without collapsing reliability and efficiency into one score.\",\n    \"figure_type\": \"paired_dot_plot\",\n    \"preferred_generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n    \"group_by\": \"region_geometry\",\n    \"metric\": \"joint_coverage_and_normalized_simplex_volume\",\n    \"split_by\": \"synthetic_condition\",\n    \"preferred_span\": \"full_width\",\n    \"target_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n    \"layout_rationale\": \"Use the full single-column 5.5-inch width, two stacked panels, and a common six-condition x-axis. Six short labels and three consistently colored series fit at 9-point final-size text; a half-width rendering would make method offsets, seed dots, and uncertainty unreadable.\",\n    \"allow_progression\": false,\n    \"max_panels\": 2,\n    \"max_panels_per_row\": 1,\n    \"max_categories_per_panel\": 6,\n    \"max_series_per_panel\": 3,\n    \"intended_footprint\": \"Approximately 5.5 by 3.4 inches plus caption, about 0.45 body page, near the start of main results.\",\n    \"content_budget\": \"Three methods, five faint seed points and one mean marker per condition; no fourth decorative series. Use a dashed 0.90 line only in the coverage panel. Volume uses the unit-simplex fraction scale. Separate the two matched controls with a vertical rule, not a chronology arrow.\",\n    \"uncertainty_display\": \"Show seed dispersion directly. Do not repurpose the released aggregate bootstrap intervals as condition-specific error bars; keep Wilson intervals and Monte Carlo errors in the detailed table or supplement.\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n      \"final.metric.marginal_coverage\",\n      \"final.metric.normalized_volume\"\n    ],\n    \"export_requirements\": \"Reproducible plotting source must export PDF and PNG at 300 DPI; LaTeX must include the PDF whenever available.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"figure_id\": \"descriptive_sign_strata\",\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"purpose\": \"Show why near-nominal marginal coverage need not imply local reliability, while preserving the distinction between descriptive diagnostics and coverage guarantees.\",\n    \"figure_type\": \"stratum_dot_plot\",\n    \"preferred_generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n    \"group_by\": \"region_geometry\",\n    \"metric\": \"empirical_joint_coverage_in_covariate_sign_stratum\",\n    \"split_by\": \"heteroskedastic_and_shifted_regimes\",\n    \"preferred_span\": \"full_width\",\n    \"target_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n    \"layout_rationale\": \"Two approximately 2.6-inch panels share one full-width 5.5-inch figure and one legend. Four short sign labels per panel and 9-point text fit without shrinking. The two regimes are scientific contrasts, not a temporal sequence.\",\n    \"allow_progression\": false,\n    \"max_panels\": 2,\n    \"max_panels_per_row\": 2,\n    \"max_categories_per_panel\": 4,\n    \"max_series_per_panel\": 3,\n    \"intended_footprint\": \"Approximately 5.5 by 2.25 inches plus caption, about 0.32 body page, in reliability and failure analysis.\",\n    \"content_budget\": \"Only the four masks x1<0, x1>=0, x2<0, x2>=0, three methods, common y-axis limits, and one nominal line. Masks overlap across covariates and are not a four-way partition. Training-defined boundary groups are not depicted as evaluated coverage groups.\",\n    \"uncertainty_display\": \"Show all five final-seed stratum rates and their means without unsupported simultaneous intervals. Empty strata are missing observations, never zero-rate plotted points; preserve the original zero-valued aggregate separately in the main text.\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n      \"final.metric.worst_stratum_coverage\"\n    ],\n    \"export_requirements\": \"Export PDF and PNG at 300 DPI from plotting source; reference PDF from LaTeX.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"figure_id\": \"search_configuration_comparison\",\n    \"required\": false,\n    \"purpose\": \"Document the limited measured comparison of residual fitting and shape routing without asserting an isolated mechanism or a final generalization result.\",\n    \"figure_type\": \"paired_dot_plot\",\n    \"preferred_generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n    \"group_by\": \"training_configuration\",\n    \"metric\": \"joint_coverage_and_normalized_simplex_volume\",\n    \"split_by\": \"search_condition\",\n    \"preferred_span\": \"full_width\",\n    \"target_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n    \"layout_rationale\": \"Supplementary single-column figure uses the same 5.5-inch two-stacked-panel design as the main comparison, preserving method labels and raw three-seed dispersion.\",\n    \"allow_progression\": false,\n    \"max_panels\": 2,\n    \"max_panels_per_row\": 1,\n    \"max_categories_per_panel\": 6,\n    \"max_series_per_panel\": 3,\n    \"intended_footprint\": \"About half a supplementary page; include only if a compact direct-comparison table does not already communicate the same evidence.\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"result.top_program_01\",\n      \"result.top_program_02\",\n      \"result.top_program_03\"\n    ],\n    \"export_requirements\": \"Use search episodes under all_programs, not the final episodes; export PDF and 300-DPI PNG from source and include PDF.\"\n  }\n]\nFINAL SUMMARY {\n  \"correct\": true,\n  \"evaluator_sha256\": \"sha256:7885573008fc5ea2e189824aca1961f7a80775701dbe7be513631d200c6c4de7\",\n  \"manifest_path\": \"work/results/r02/codex/20261107_044437/final_evaluation/final_manifest.json\",\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"combined_score\": 0.8835919142358097,\n    \"coverage_gap_vs_euclidean\": -0.001440972222222218,\n    \"coverage_gap_vs_ilr\": 0.025052083333333332,\n    \"marginal_coverage\": 0.8941579861111111,\n    \"normalized_volume\": 0.5446175893147787,\n    \"volume_gain_vs_euclidean\": -0.03463134765625,\n    \"volume_gain_vs_ilr\": 0.049602508544921875,\n    \"worst_stratum_coverage\": 0.0\n  },\n  \"outcome\": \"qualified\",\n  \"program_tree_sha256\": \"sha256:0acba4fc77ee8d3b8d0352fb6548f8ae2aefa077d64315ca2abcd037527c3a63\",\n  \"results_tree_sha256\": \"sha256:b3924f0c7fc6b8414475a88e279bfb06ec4fe6566987f426fac956ae39f1e4e1\",\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"task_tree_sha256\": \"sha256:7a926d279d983569c28cd59e8e47451170af57d53bc2aac3060e52bb85985e1b\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
