ncentered standardized-residual second moments with identity weight 8 and group-to-pooled weight 32; training-frozen predicted-minimum-component tertiles and right-sided routing select a Cholesky factor. Shapes are not group calibration.', ['source_evidence/adaptive.py:90-131', 'source_evidence/adaptive.py:190-198'], ('LedoitWolf2004', 'Chen2010'))\n+method_claim('For fewer than four training rows a full-data location, zero variance coefficients and identity group factors are used; full-sized evaluated data do not exercise this branch.', ['source_evidence/adaptive.py:103-114'])\n+claim('Independent score calibration uses ceil((ncal+1)(1-alpha)) with infinity if the rank exceeds ncal; exchangeable frozen-score rank argument gives marginal coverage at least 1-alpha, not a realized finite-test or conditional bound.', [EPISODES, 'ref.Lei2018', 'ref.Angelopoulos2021'], ('Lei2018', 'Angelopoulos2021'), ('source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:859-864',))\n+claim('Each final condition has 4096 training, 2048 calibration and 3840 test rows; calibration rank 1845; seed labels 1009,2027,3049,4051,5059.', [EPISODES], paths=['source_evidence/final_resource_manifest.json', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:34-45'])\n+claim('Complete synthetic generator parameters and row provenance in the main text and Supplementary Information are transcribed from inspected code and frozen manifests, including all Gaussian scales, nonlinear means, Dirichlet concentrations, redraw limits and shift settings.', [EPISODES], paths=['source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:776-814', 'source_evidence/final_resource_manifest.json'])\n+claim('C5 replaces all C2 covariates with zero; C6 cyclically deranges only training covariate rows. These are shared-response matched controls rather than independent tasks.', [EPISODES], paths=['source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:1007-1036'])\n+claim('Common-volume fractions use 64 evenly indexed anchors and 4096 Dirichlet(1,...,1) probes per anchor; shared membership probes and sample-variance formulas give conditional paired integration errors.', [EPISODES], paths=['source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:907-938', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:1033-1036', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:1206-1229'])\n+claim('Wilson 95% intervals condition on fitted/calibrated regions and finite test data; conditional Monte Carlo errors do not include fitting or anchor variability. These differ from seed-block bootstrap uncertainty.', [EPISODES, 'ref.Wilson1927'], ('Wilson1927', 'Efron1979', 'Davison1997'), ('source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:871-880', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:907-938'))\n+claim('The supplementary utility formula is 1-0.8*max(0,0.9-coverage)/0.9-0.2*volume, equal-weighted across specified cases and seeds; it is not a hard coverage constraint or proper distribution forecast score.', [EPISODES], ('Gneiting2007',), ('source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:932-938', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:1245-1263'))\n+\n+claim('There are three measured development configurations with shared seeds 101,211,307 and counts 2048/1024/2048; auxiliary figures use development data only. The single-split contrast bundles residual data allocation and full-training location refitting.', ['result.total_attempts', 'result.total_evaluated_programs', 'result.top_program_01', 'result.top_program_02', 'result.top_program_03'], paths=['source_evidence/search_resource_manifest.json', 'source_evidence/single_split.py:108-131', 'source_evidence/adaptive.py:108-131', 'derived/search_comparison.json'])\n+claim('Interpolated covariance uses frozen training quantiles 1/6,1/2,5/6, averages duplicate anchors, clamps endpoints, convexly interpolates shapes and applies Cholesky afterward; no consistent advantage is established by the retained development comparison.', ['result.top_program_01', 'result.top_program_02', 'result.top_program_03'], paths=['source_evidence/interpolated.py:121-151', 'source_evidence/interpolated.py:200-240', 'derived/search_comparison.json'])\n+claim('No isolated shrinkage, Hellinger, group-calibration, structural-zero, real-data or full-data-refit evaluation supports broader attribution; shifted conditions alter the sampling law and cannot validate exchangeability-based or conditional claims.', [EPISODES, 'result.top_program_01', 'result.top_program_02', 'result.top_program_03'], ('Tibshirani2019', 'Barber2023', 'Barber2021Limits'), ('source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:776-814',))\n+durations = SUMMARY['duration_seconds']\n+claim(f'Observed retained seed duration totals range from {min(durations):.9f} to {max(durations):.9f} seconds; not end-to-end or hardware-specific reproduction timings.', [EPISODES])\n+claim('The evaluated NumPy requirement is 2.2.6; exact resource recreation is not possible from public seed labels alone because private entropy is used. Replay requires frozen NPZ arrays and manifests. Readable evaluated copies, not hashes alone, support implementation facts.', [EPISODES, 'result.top_program_01'], paths=['source_evidence/requirements.txt', 'source_evidence/manifest.json', 'source_evidence/final_resource_manifest.json', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:768-814'])\n+\n+claim('Foundational related-work distinctions: compositional log-ratio representation and logistic-normal modeling; regression split calibration; quantile adaptation; label-set prediction; cross-fitting versus jackknife+; marginal versus conditional validity; shift correction; proper probabilistic scores.', ['ref.' + key for key in ['Aitchison1982','Egozcue2003','AitchisonShen1980','Pawlowsky2011','Vovk2005','Papadopoulos2002','Lei2018','Romano2019','Romano2020','Ding2023','Barber2021Jackknife','Vovk2012','Barber2021Limits','Tibshirani2019','Barber2023','Gneiting2007']], ['Aitchison1982','Egozcue2003','AitchisonShen1980','Pawlowsky2011','Vovk2005','Papadopoulos2002','Lei2018','Romano2019','Romano2020','Ding2023','Barber2021Jackknife','Vovk2012','Barber2021Limits','Tibshirani2019','Barber2023','Gneiting2007'])\n+\n+(ROOT / 'claims_grounding.json').write_text(json.dumps({'claims': CLAIMS}, indent=2) + '\\\\n')\n+print(f'Wrote {len(CLAIMS)} grounded claim groups.')\n*** Add File: REPRODUCIBILITY.md\n+# Reproduction and evidence guide\n+\n+## Scope and files\n+\n+This manuscript analyzes retained evaluator outputs; manuscript preparation did not run a new model evaluation. \"'`paper_data.json` is the read-only numerical registry. `claims_grounding.json` maps manuscript claims to its stable source identifiers and to bibliographic provenance. Additional `implementation_evidence` entries identify readable source locations, not merely hashes. `source_evidence/manifest.json` records the exact copied source files and hashes. The final evaluation is completed and qualified, but the scientific coverage/volume failures remain in the main paper.\n+\n+The study is entirely synthetic. There is no downloaded real dataset, account requirement, or third-party dataset-license acceptance. Frozen resource files and their generation details are listed in `task/resources/final/manifest.json` and `task/resources/search/manifest.json`; the `task` link points to the accompanying task distribution. Preserve these directories when moving the submission. Do not treat public seed labels as sufficient to regenerate the corpus: private per-resource entropy is used and the frozen NPZ arrays are necessary for exact replay.\n+\n+## Environment\n+\n+The evaluated scientific dependency is `numpy==2.2.6`, as recorded in `source_evidence/requirements.txt`. The evaluated implementations are Python and standard-library code plus NumPy. The evaluator additionally requires Linux CPU-affinity/resource limits and its Landlock/seccomp isolation facilities. The original historical Python patch version and exact hardware were not retained in the evidence registry; manuscript construction uses the environment recorded in `paper_environment.json`, without claiming it was the historical evaluation environment.\n+\n+For figures/tables and PDF inspection, install packages from `requirements-paper.txt` into a private environment outside this manuscript directory. A working TeX Live installation, BibTeX, and Poppler `pdftotext` are needed for compilation/validation. Do not put package trees in the manuscript workspace.\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m venv /tmp/composition-paper-env\n+/tmp/composition-paper-env/bin/pip install -r requirements-paper.txt\n+/tmp/composition-paper-env/bin/python build_artifacts.py\n+/tmp/composition-paper-env/bin/python build_claims.py\n+pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error paper.tex\n+bibtex paper\n+pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error paper.tex\n+pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error paper.tex\n+```\n+\n+The plotting script preserves an orchestrator-rendered overview when `.concept_figure_complete` exists or a nonempty overview prompt log is present. It never overwrites that rendered asset. Before orchestration the overview PNG is a compile-safe pending placeholder; the finished overview is supplied synchronously by the outer workflow, not claimed as a finished diagram by this writing step.\n+\n+## Scientific replay (not performed during writing)\n+\n+Use the distributed final evaluator and selected source, not a rewritten approximation:\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m venv /tmp/composition-eval-env\n+/tmp/composition-eval-env/bin/pip install -r source_evidence/requirements.txt\n+TASK_SOURCE_DIR=\"$PWD/task\" /tmp/composition-eval-env/bin/python task/evaluate_final.py '\"\\\\\n+  --program_path \\\"\"'$PWD/source_evidence/adaptive.py\" '\"\\\\\n+  --results_dir /tmp/composition-replay\n+\"'```\n+\n+The evaluator copies the source directory into an isolated process. For minimal replay packaging, copy `source_evidence/adaptive.py` alone into a clean temporary source directory and use that path if the full source-evidence directory exceeds the evaluator'\"'s file limits. Preserve the original final NPZ files with matching manifest hashes. This replay command is documented from the inspected CLI and is not asserted to have been rerun here. Seed labels, counts and all other settings are read from the frozen evaluator/resource manifests.\n+\n+Observed retained per-seed episode duration totals span 6.46–7.59 seconds. These are not full end-to-end timings, installation timings or hardware-specific forecasts. No new wall-time estimate is fabricated. Figure construction and literature lookup are separate from those measured durations.\n+\n+## Output map\n+\n+| Manuscript object | Construction | Inputs |\n+|---|---|---|\n+| Overview | Outer \"'`generate-concept-figure` workflow | `paper_strategy.json`, finished `paper.tex` |\n+| Condition comparison | `build_artifacts.py` | final episode coverage and volume |\n+| Sign-stratum comparison | `build_artifacts.py` | C2/C4 final episode sign-mask rates |\n+| Auxiliary configuration comparison | `build_artifacts.py` | three development configurations'\"' episode records |\n+| Condition-mean table | \"'`build_artifacts.py` → `tables/condition_means.tex` | final episodes |\n+| Complete seed table | `build_artifacts.py` → `tables/seed_results.tex` | final episodes including Wilson intervals and MC SE |\n+| Aggregate contrast table | `paper.tex` | registered final metrics and released paired bootstrap intervals |\n+| Operational-check table | `paper.tex` | final episode checks and independent qualification fields |\n+\n+`derived/complete_results.json` preserves per-anchor volumes, all sign-mask rates, radii/ranks, point errors and paired integration errors. Empty constant-input negative-sign masks keep their original zero encodings and are separately flagged as empty, never treated as measured zero coverage. `derived/summary.json` contains deterministic means and sample SDs across retained seeds, not newly simulated results. `derived/search_comparison.json` is strictly development-data evidence. All quantitative plots have PDF and 300-DPI PNG outputs, and LaTeX uses the vector PDF. Adjacent provenance sidecars point to actual source files.\n+\n+## Literature independence and reading scope\n+\n+No broad task-identifying query or citation chaining was performed during manuscript writing. A supplied bibliography containing many application-specific compositional citations was replaced with direct-identifier lookups of foundational methodology. Original metadata, official arXiv abstracts and selected downloaded papers are under `literature/`; `reading.json`, `reading_report.txt`, and `references_provenance.json` state the actual scope of inspection. Selected conformal papers were inspected through their opening methodological pages; other entries were read at metadata/abstract level, not asserted to have undergone full-text review. Publisher access failures are retained rather than hidden. This is not a novelty certification or systematic review.\n+\n+No prohibited-source encounter was identified during this manuscript-writing step. This statement does not certify unobserved earlier retrieval. If a later reader encounters prohibited material, stop reading it and append the URL, location and extent of exposure to the log rather than using it.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+Use the staged `validate-paper` scripts for source/citation checks, claim/provenance checks, figure schema/readability checks, compilation and visible Supplementary Information checks. Use the `scientific-evidence` verifier for dangling-reference checks. `validation_report.json` records the performed checks and any environmental limitation; it must not be interpreted as a substitute for a human scientific review. No private-entropy generation, new component ablation or missing gate diagnostic is inferred from a passing artifact check.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\n/tmp/paper-tools/bin/python build_claims.py\n/tmp/paper-tools/bin/pip freeze > requirements-paper.txt\n/tmp/paper-tools/bin/python - <<'\"'PY'\nimport sys,json,platform\nfrom pathlib import Path\nPath('paper_environment.json').write_text(json.dumps({'purpose':'manuscript artifact construction, not the historical evaluation environment','python':sys.version,'platform':platform.platform(),'evaluated_dependency':'numpy==2.2.6'},indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Wrote 47 grounded claim groups.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
