{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_102","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"/tmp/apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n--- paper.tex\n+++ paper.tex\n@@ -236,1 +236,1 @@\n-\\\\includegraphics[width=\\\\textwidth]{figures/coverage_volume_by_condition.pdf}\n+\\\\includegraphics[width=\\\\textwidth]{figures/coverage_volume_by_regime.pdf}\n@@ -175,1 +175,6 @@\n \\\\subsection{Common-Measure Volume and Uncertainty}\n+Development selection used a fixed utility that penalizes a shortfall from nominal coverage and the volume fraction: \"'$U('\"\\\\widehat c,\\\\widehat V)=1-0.8\\\\max(0,0.9-\\\\widehat c)/0.9-0.2\\\\widehat V\"'$. The objective averages across the specified conditions and seeds. It is not a constrained optimization requiring coverage to meet the target: a sufficiently compact region can offset a coverage shortfall in this utility. Conversely, coverage above the target receives no extra reward. The configuration selected by this objective therefore requires a separate scientific assessment of its components. We do not identify selection under that trade-off with satisfaction of every performance target. All observed conditions, including those unfavorable to the frozen configuration, remain in the final comparison.\n+% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L932-L938]]\n+% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L1245-L1263]]\n+\n@@ -351,1 +356,5 @@\n '\"\\\\section{Discussion and Limitations}\n+The information-removal controls help interpret compactness without establishing a mechanism. With constant covariates, a fitted region cannot distinguish test locations from their inputs, so a wide region reflects the heterogeneous response distribution left after removing that information. With deranged training pairs, the calibration/test association is unchanged but the fitted relationship is degraded. Independent calibration can still adjust a frozen score to the resulting marginal residual distribution. Neither control is equivalent to testing whether the intact model has recovered a particular conditional law. In particular, their near-nominal marginal coverage does not validate the intact model's local reliability. The useful contrast is the loss of compactness when predictive training information is removed, not a proof that every adaptive shape factor is necessary.\n+% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L1007-L1036]]\n+% @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes]]\n+\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\n/tmp/paper-tools/bin/python build_artifacts.py > /tmp/artifact_summary.json\n/tmp/paper-tools/bin/python build_claims.py\npython .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_tex_refs.py --tex paper.tex --bib references.bib\nPYTHONPATH=/workspace/task/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages /tmp/paper-tools/bin/python .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_figures.py --paper-dir .\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
